<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation" xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml" xmlns:s="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib">
 <s:String x:Key="buildTitle">Your material. Your structures.</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildIntro">Aim at material, save it as a replacement and place it with the building hammer.</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildReadTitle">Capture material with the pickaxe</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildReadHint">Take the pickaxe → aim at terrain or a building block → press your capture shortcut. The target is enabled as a replacement immediately.</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildRead">Remember material in crosshair</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildIdLabel">Material ID (1–255)</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildReplaceTitle">Replace material</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildReplaceHint">When replacement is enabled, the building material placed with the hammer is replaced by your selection.</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildApply">Apply selection</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildFavoriteName">Name for your favorite</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildFavorites">Your material favorites</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildSaveFavorite">Save as favorite</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildRemoveFavorite">Remove favorite</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildUseFavorite">Use favorite</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="objectTitle">A world full of possibilities.</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectIntro">Capture fences, doors, plants and decorations and place them as new objects.</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectAimTitle">Capture an object with the pickaxe</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectAimHint">Take the pickaxe → aim at an object → press your capture shortcut. The target is enabled as a replacement immediately. Then place your source object.</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectRemember">Remember object in crosshair</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectUseAim">Use remembered object as replacement</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectCatalogTitle">Object catalog</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectSearchHint">Search catalog</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectOnlyFavorites">Favorites only</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectUseSelected">Use selection as replacement</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectFavorite">Toggle favorite</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectSourceTitle">Source object</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectImport">Update catalog from game files</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectTechnical">Also show creatures, effects and technical templates</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectAnySource">Currently selected placeable object</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectFixedSource">Fixed source object</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectUseSelectedSource">Use catalog selection as fixed source</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectCaptureSource">Last normally placed object as source</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectSourceHint">For a fixed source, choose a workbench, vase or another object. To capture a new source, disable replacement and place it once normally.</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectReplaceTitle">Replace object</s:String><s:String x:Key="objectReplaceHint">Your source object is replaced by this selection when placing. The clear shortcut disables replacement.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="buildingConnect">Connect to Enshrouded</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildingDisconnected">Connect to Enshrouded before capturing or replacing.</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildingWaiting">Waiting for a target in the game …</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildingNoTarget">No selection yet</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildingOn">REPLACEMENT ON</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildingOff">REPLACEMENT OFF</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildingSourceAny">Source: your current selection in the game</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildPreserveTitle">Keep building material</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildPreserveHint">Your materials remain when placing building blocks and objects. The normal material check in the building menu stays active. The game may return material when dismantling. First test version for your local world.</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildPreserveOn">KEEP MATERIAL ON</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildPreserveOff">KEEP MATERIAL OFF</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildFreeTitle">Free building</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildFreeHint">The material check is bypassed when placing building blocks and placeable objects. Normal replacement remains controlled separately. First test version for your local world.</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildFreeOn">FREE BUILDING ON</s:String><s:String x:Key="buildFreeOff">FREE BUILDING OFF</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="craftTitle">Your workshop. Your supplies.</s:String><s:String x:Key="craftIntro">Crafting and recipes at the blacksmith and other NPCs.</s:String><s:String x:Key="craftFavorite">Save as favorite</s:String><s:String x:Key="craftPreserveTitle">Keep ingredients</s:String><s:String x:Key="craftPreserveHint">Craft available recipes and keep your ingredients. Required materials must be present in the crafting menu. First test version for crafting and NPC recipes.</s:String><s:String x:Key="craftPreserveOn">KEEP INGREDIENTS ON</s:String><s:String x:Key="craftPreserveOff">KEEP INGREDIENTS OFF</s:String><s:String x:Key="craftTestHint">Test by crafting a recipe: ingredients should remain and the finished item should be added. Turn it off to compare normal consumption.</s:String><s:String x:Key="craftNextTitle">Planned next</s:String><s:String x:Key="craftNextHint">Craft without ingredients, unlock all recipes and adjustable production speed. Ovens, dryers and similar stations will be checked separately.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="objectReplacementLabel">Active replacement</s:String><s:String x:Key="nearbyTitle">Objects near you</s:String><s:String x:Key="nearbyHint">Scans loaded objects and filters them by distance from you. Change the radius before each scan.</s:String><s:String x:Key="nearbyRadiusLabel">Radius (m)</s:String><s:String x:Key="nearbyScan">Scan nearby</s:String><s:String x:Key="nearbyEmpty">No scan yet</s:String><s:String x:Key="nearbyLoading">Reading objects …</s:String><s:String x:Key="nearbyUse">Activate selection as replacement</s:String><s:String x:Key="nearbyChoose">Choose an object from the nearby scan first.</s:String><s:String x:Key="nearbyCount">different object templates in the loaded area</s:String><s:String x:Key="nearbyReady">Area read. Choose an object and activate it as replacement.</s:String><s:String x:Key="equipmentTitle">Your equipment. For every adventure.</s:String><s:String x:Key="equipmentIntro">Keep tools and weapons; more inventory functions will follow.</s:String><s:String x:Key="durabilityTitle">Infinite durability</s:String><s:String x:Key="durabilityHint">Weapons and tools lose no durability when used. Already damaged or broken items are not repaired; normal repairs remain possible. First test version.</s:String><s:String x:Key="durabilityOn">KEEP DURABILITY ON</s:String><s:String x:Key="durabilityOff">KEEP DURABILITY OFF</s:String><s:String x:Key="durabilityTestHint">Test by mining with a tool and attacking with a weapon. Compare durability before and after, then disable it and check normal wear.</s:String>
<s:String x:Key="dismantleTitle">Dismantle overridden objects · Test</s:String>
<s:String x:Key="dismantleHint">Enable before placement. Intended to make newly overridden fences, doors and other world props removable normally. Applies only to the selected replacement. Existing objects remain unchanged. Material refunds and in-game behavior still need testing.</s:String>
</ResourceDictionary>
